  "architecture": {
    "crossing": "Only a started real-playback session can dispatch. Forward uses previous < cue <= current; reverse uses current <= cue < previous. Frame drops collect every crossing in deterministic time/event-ID order.",
    "scrubbing": "Scrubbing is an exact no-dispatch path. It neither authorizes an operation nor mutates the execution ledger.",
    "identity": "Flypath ID, immutable published revision, requested revision, session ID, requester ID, and non-local session token are explicit inputs. A revision mismatch fails the complete batch closed.",
    "authorization": "Non-local operations require an enabled post-clone binding, exact adapter/version and region, resolved target, bounded range, named permission, positive rate budget, and policy approval for Server World scope.",
    "payload": "Payload shape and byte bounds are validated before EventCuePlanValidV1 is published. Per-frame selection/authorization treats the compiled payload as opaque and cannot interpret or execute it; any later server adapter must revalidate the bounded payload at its authoritative RPC boundary.",
    "ledger": "Execution authority is keyed by Event ID, loop iteration, and direction. Once-per-session and manual-reset Cues remain disarmed across loops; every-loop Cues may execute once per loop and direction. Only adapter success commits: a fresh explicit bounded-adapter receipt must have succeeded=true and code executed or state_satisfied. Three private candidate arrays are validated before the three authoritative ledger arrays publish atomically.",
    "failure": "Authorization returns stable typed rejection codes. It cannot execute a fallback operation, replace a binding, or claim ledger success.",
    "forbidden": "Arbitrary actor pointers, class names, function names, reflection dispatch, CameraTransform, camera/body/gimbal authorship, native camera mutation, repository mutation, HUD, polished UI, cooking, deployment, and synchronized performance are absent."
  },
  "acceptance": {
    "offline": "Executable reference tests cover deterministic skipped-frame crossings, reverse order, scrub isolation, repeat policies, manifest tampering, revision/session/binding/region/range/permission/rate failures, default-disabled Server World scope, and success-only ledger publication.",
    "live": "Deterministic full/paste graphs and independent interpreters must match the reference before one-editor configuration. Warm runtime and player-owned PIE must prove local dispatch, typed remote rejection, scrub zero-dispatch, loop/reverse behavior, cancellation cleanup, exact defaults, guarded shutdown, reverse sync, and cold load."
  }
}
